I decided to ascend a ranger. The first one died quickly, the second one 
turned out to be a barbarian (mistake when picking the role), but the 
third one went well.

Actually, it was a mixed blessing: I found a BoH in the mines and an "oR 
in Sokoban, but found no special cloaks, helmets or gloves until in 
Gehennom, and only worthless boots. I also picked up teleportitis early 
from a tengu. Oh, and I found a wand of wishing in Sokoban (0:3 even) 
but didn't use it, since I was going wishless (and genoless/polypileless).

I had Stormbringer at +5 and a stack of +5 daggers, but no MR. I looked 
through the entire dungeon, and even went into Gehennom until I started 
meeting high level liches. Then I remembered priests sometimes have a 
CoMR and the priest in the VotD was kind enough to donate his.

So I proceeded into Gehennom. I had AC -14 (I had found only two scrolls 
of enchant armor, and hadn't found gray or silver dragon scales yet, so 
I wasn't wearing DSM) which is low, but I've gone into Gehennom with 
less and ascended. But I was also an elf. I usually play humans, and the 
18 max strength was bugging me, since I am quite a packrat. So I started 
to get burdened, and didn't do anything about it. I pushed on, and on 
level 46, I entered one of the fake wizard towers.

A lich was there, and summoned monsters all around me. Before I knew it, 
I was at 7 HP (I had about 100 max). I couldn't engrave, since I was 
levitating. I had offensive wands, but there were too many monsters. I 
had only an uncursed ?oTele, which doesn't work on that level. I had 
stupidly put my !oFH in my bag. I tried to take it out, knowing I'd die, 
which is did.

This is the furthest down I've ever died. I was drowned once at the 
castle, and apart from that, I never died below level 12. Oh well, at 
least I gave hearse users a nice bones file...

